READ-ONLY measurement round. Nothing under `srmech/` is touched; two files land
under `docs/srmech/notes/`.

WHAT rc426 LEFT OPEN, AND WHAT THIS ANSWERS
rc426 F7 measured THAT the chart carries strictly more than the carrier — 35
chart symbols onto 12 carrier values, interval agreement 1225/1225, backward map
not injective, "the surplus is SPELLING". It did not say what that surplus IS.

It is the kernel coset of a surjection from a free abelian group, restricted to a
declared window — and srmech already ships the op that enumerates it.

* The 35 letter+accidental symbols are in BIJECTION with a CONTIGUOUS 35-wide
  window of the chain generated by 7 in Z/12, and their preimage histogram comes
  back bit-identical to F7's {2:1, 3:11}. rc426's `STEP_MAP = (0,2,4,5,7,9,11)`,
  which its own comment calls "the chart's ONLY convention", is REPRODUCED here
  from (n=12, g=7, c0=-1, a=7) — so that map is the image of a three-parameter
  declaration, not a convention.
* `lift_fibre(mod_mul(mod_inv(g,n), p, n), n, W)` equals the brute chain fibre on
  6462 of 6462 cells across ten moduli and every unit generator of each. A
  spelling-fibre op is therefore REJECTED: it would re-ship
  `srmech.math.covering.lift_fibre`.
* Recoverability, measured three ways with a control that passes: NOT from the
  chart declaration (0 of 12 values uniquely spelled), NOT from carrier context
  (an 8-note sequence admits 6561 spellings and the count GROWS), YES from a
  cover-valued datum. The modifier-free control returns {1:12}, so the
  instrument can say "recoverable" and does.

THE LEAK TEST HAS A GENERATOR-SHAPED HOLE
A probe that accepts a modulus, is total over the sweep, returns 10 distinct
answers as n moves and contains no literal 12 — and hard-wires the fifth — is
filed FRAME-PARAMETRIC by rc426's F12b, i.e. clean. It is not clean: the
generator is the datum that FORCES the alphabet size, measured as
`a = g^-1 mod n` on 0 failures across every (n, unit g). So "seven letter names"
is not the Western datum; `g = 7` is, and seven follows. This is a BOUND on the
committed F12b instrument, not a refutation — every verdict it returned stands.

TWO MORE THINGS FELL OUT WITHOUT BEING ASKED FOR
* The key signature is two shipped calls and a Class-K read: accidental count =
  magnitude(least-magnitude representative of `g^-1 * t mod n`), agreeing with an
  independent rotation search 12 of 12 and reproducing F14b's
  `degrees_needing_a_modifier = 1` at shift 7. Sorting by it RECOVERS the circle
  of fifths. At the tritone the two representatives TIE — the enharmonic
  ambiguity reappearing one level up, as an ambiguity between keys.
* `octonion_frame_read` shares the clef SHAPE on three clauses and SEPARATES on
  the fourth: the clef atlas is a principal Z-bundle (transitive AND free), the
  28 frames are a fibred set, 7 lines x 4 units, with a stabiliser of order 2.
  FORM, not identity.

THE ACTION FAMILY CHARTS A DIFFERENT CARRIER, AND IT IS RANK 2
Reproducing F23 exactly (78 -> 37, {1:10, 2:13, 3:14}): for a regular tuning the
action->pitch map is additive on 21 of 21 pairs, the kernel is generated by
(1,-5) and every tablature fibre is a coset of it; for an irregular one
additivity fails at 5 of 21 and no kernel exists. Controls behave — one course
reports NO loss, all-unison a flat 6-fold fibre.

Sourcing untouched: the rc426 per-tradition tiers are taken as given and not
re-asserted; tuning vectors are labelled MODEL PARAMETERS, never tradition
claims.

